# Pin the runner image so a local `act` run is reproducible. act-latest is the
# medium image: it carries docker and the common toolchain without pulling the
# ~20GB full-size runner.
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest
--container-daemon-socket /var/run/docker.sock
# act force-pulls the runner on every run by default, which is a ~1GB round trip
# per iteration. This still pulls when the image is absent.
--pull=false
# Never put a token or a Docker Hub credential here - this file is tracked.
# The build job hard-disables publishing whenever ACT is set, so a local run
# cannot reach the registry even if one is passed on the command line.
